      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Nine reference images, one scene with sound: FastH3-Omni weaves people, outfits, an object, places and a style into a single 8-second shot. The three people are Pictures 1 to 3, the marble statue is Picture 4, the samurai armour and the gold jacket are Pictures 5 and 6, which the fisherman and the gardener wear, the beach is Picture 7, on a billboard, the neon street is Picture 8, where the scene takes place, and the anime character is Picture 9, on a poster.\n\nWhat FastH3-Omni can do:\n\u2022 Reference images: up to 3 in real time, and up to 9 when real-time speed isn't needed, as in this render.\n\u2022 Audio input: up to 3 sounds guide voices and soundtracks, and the prompt writes the speech, sound effects and music.\n\u2022 First-to-last frame: start a clip on a first frame (image), end it on a last frame (last_image), or both, with at least one picture beside them.\n\nWriting prompts for FastH3-Omni:\n\u2022 Name inputs in angle brackets: <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>, \u2026 in picture-socket order, and say what each one is and where it goes in the scene.\n\u2022 Tie each picture to one thing on screen: a person, what they wear, an object, the place, or a sign or poster in the scene.\n\u2022 With many pictures, details can cross between them: in our run the fisherman picked up the samurai's topknot for part of the shot.\n\nFastH3-Omni prompt guide: https://docs.reactor.inc/model-api-reference/fast-h3-omni/prompt-guide\n\nSet your Reactor API key in this plugin's config.ini."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "Nine reference images, one scene with sound: FastH3-Omni weaves people, outfits, an object, places and a style into a single 8-second shot. The three people are Pictures 1 to 3, the marble statue is Picture 4, the samurai armour and the gold jacket are Pictures 5 and 6, which the fisherman and the gardener wear, the beach is Picture 7, on a billboard, the neon street is Picture 8, where the scene takes place, and the anime character is Picture 9, on a poster.\n\nWhat FastH3-Omni can do:\n\u2022 Reference images: up to 3 in real time, and up to 9 when real-time speed isn't needed, as in this render.\n\u2022 Audio input: up to 3 sounds guide voices and soundtracks, and the prompt writes the speech, sound effects and music.\n\u2022 First-to-last frame: start a clip on a first frame (image), end it on a last frame (last_image), or both, with at least one picture beside them.\n\nWriting prompts for FastH3-Omni:\n\u2022 Name inputs in angle brackets: <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>, \u2026 in picture-socket order, and say what each one is and where it goes in the scene.\n\u2022 Tie each picture to one thing on screen: a person, what they wear, an object, the place, or a sign or poster in the scene.\n\u2022 With many pictures, details can cross between them: in our run the fisherman picked up the samurai's topknot for part of the shot.\n\nFastH3-Omni prompt guide: https://docs.reactor.inc/model-api-reference/fast-h3-omni/prompt-guide\n\nSet your Reactor API key in this plugin's config.ini."
      },
